<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>First-line medicine for limb tremor, chosen with movement disorders neurology: propranolol extended-release 60 mg each morning from the four-week visit; check resting heart rate and seated and standing blood pressure at every visit, ask about wheeze, fatigue, low mood, and lightheadedness, and do not stop it suddenly; primidone, started at 12.5 to 25 mg at bedtime, is held as the alternative or add-on, with checks for sedation, unsteadiness, and falls. Guideline: Evidence-based guideline update: treatment of essential tremor: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2011); Practice parameter: therapies for essential tremor: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2005); MDS evidence-based review of treatments for essential tremor (2019) [S]</item><item>Movement disorders neurology consultation to confirm the diagnosis against the MDS consensus classification, choose treatment, and advise on head and voice tremor. Guideline: Evidence-based guideline update: treatment of essential tremor: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2011); Consensus Statement on the classification of tremors, from the task force on tremor of the International Parkinson and Movement Disorder Society (2018) [S]</item><item>Speech-language therapy for voice tremor, and occupational therapy for adaptive aids (weighted utensils, lidded cups, thick-barreled pens). Guideline: Evidence-based guideline update: treatment of essential tremor: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2011); MDS evidence-based review of treatments for essential tremor (2019) [S]</item><item>Monitor at every visit: TETRAS performance and daily-living subscales, spiral drawing and handwriting, heart rate and standing blood pressure on propranolol, side effects, falls, and drugs that worsen tremor; yearly: examination for signs beyond tremor, mood, cognition, and an AGS Beers Criteria medication review. Focused ultrasound thalamotomy or deep brain stimulation is considered only if disabling limb tremor persists after adequate trials of propranolol and primidone. Guideline: Evidence-based guideline update: treatment of essential tremor: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2011); Consensus Statement on the classification of tremors, from the task force on tremor of the International Parkinson and Movement Disorder Society (2018); A Randomized Trial of Focused Ultrasound Thalamotomy for Essential Tremor (2016); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, general items for older adults (no essential tremor monograph) (2026) [S]</item><item>Advance care planning: name a health care agent and record goals of care at the annual wellness visit. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, general items for older adults (no essential tremor monograph) (2026) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
